1
00:00:00,043 --> 00:00:01,044
GridBot Builder.

2
00:00:01,634 --> 00:00:02,784
GridBot Blueprint.

3
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:04,074
Lesson one.

4
00:00:04,626 --> 00:00:05,355
Introduction.

5
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:07,616
Education only.

6
00:00:08,175 --> 00:00:09,489
Not financial advice.

7
00:00:10,009 --> 00:00:12,061
This is general information and

8
00:00:12,061 --> 00:00:14,264
doesn't consider your objectives,

9
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:16,164
financial situation or needs.

10
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:18,883
Crypto, a digital coin, is high risk;

11
00:00:18,883 --> 00:00:21,319
you could lose all the money you put in.

12
00:00:21,839 --> 00:00:23,904
Past performance is not a reliable

13
00:00:23,904 --> 00:00:25,613
indicator of future results.

14
00:00:26,663 --> 00:00:29,056
The prices are public historical prices

15
00:00:29,056 --> 00:00:31,234
at the end of each day, marked Example.

16
00:00:32,367 --> 00:00:34,266
No order is sent from this lesson.

17
00:00:35,265 --> 00:00:37,241
By the end of this series you will

18
00:00:37,241 --> 00:00:39,291
understand what a grid bot, a small

19
00:00:39,291 --> 00:00:41,340
program that places these orders

20
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:43,243
for you, does, when it can capture

21
00:00:43,243 --> 00:00:44,854
bounces, and where it loses.

22
00:00:45,374 --> 00:00:47,384
You will know how to plan one, test

23
00:00:47,384 --> 00:00:49,284
it on paper, run it, check it, and

24
00:00:49,284 --> 00:00:51,331
change the capital you give to bots

25
00:00:51,331 --> 00:00:53,193
only under written risk rules.

26
00:00:53,713 --> 00:00:55,110
This is education, not

27
00:00:55,110 --> 00:00:56,429
a promise of results.

28
00:00:56,949 --> 00:00:58,560
Price often moves sideways,

29
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,310
bouncing between the same top

30
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:02,061
and bottom instead of leaving.

31
00:01:02,581 --> 00:01:04,290
A grid is a ladder of waiting

32
00:01:04,290 --> 00:01:06,000
orders, called limit orders,

33
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,487
built for that bouncing.

34
00:01:08,007 --> 00:01:09,850
When price runs one way and stays

35
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:12,029
there, the grid has nothing left to do.

36
00:01:12,410 --> 00:01:14,163
And if price falls through the

37
00:01:14,163 --> 00:01:15,846
bottom, coin means the crypto

38
00:01:15,846 --> 00:01:17,669
itself, and you are left holding

39
00:01:17,669 --> 00:01:19,401
the coin, and it is worth less.

40
00:01:20,331 --> 00:01:21,672
By the end you will know

41
00:01:21,672 --> 00:01:22,957
what a grid bot places.

42
00:01:24,086 --> 00:01:26,165
You will see that idea on

43
00:01:26,165 --> 00:01:28,140
one real path from 2023.

44
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:30,848
You will be able to say the

45
00:01:30,848 --> 00:01:32,301
stop rule in one sentence.

46
00:01:33,255 --> 00:01:35,101
When a chart says Example, it

47
00:01:35,101 --> 00:01:36,946
means a real past price used

48
00:01:36,946 --> 00:01:38,792
as an example, not a forecast.

49
00:01:39,842 --> 00:01:41,084
Crypto is a digital

50
00:01:41,084 --> 00:01:42,481
asset, such as bitcoin.

51
00:01:43,001 --> 00:01:44,677
You do not need to have bought

52
00:01:44,677 --> 00:01:45,962
any before this lesson.

53
00:01:46,341 --> 00:01:48,308
An exchange is the website or app

54
00:01:48,308 --> 00:01:50,640
where you swap Australian dollars for

55
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:52,681
crypto, and crypto back to dollars.

56
00:01:53,201 --> 00:01:54,877
This course does not name one,

57
00:01:54,877 --> 00:01:56,553
and it does not send an order.

58
00:01:57,298 --> 00:01:58,862
Cash is money you can spend.

59
00:01:59,264 --> 00:02:00,886
Here that means dollars, or a

60
00:02:00,886 --> 00:02:02,650
dollar-pegged token, treated

61
00:02:02,650 --> 00:02:04,060
like cash in this lesson.

62
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:05,596
The peg can break.

63
00:02:06,116 --> 00:02:08,308
Coin is the crypto, such as bitcoin.

64
00:02:09,358 --> 00:02:11,704
An order is an instruction to buy or sell.

65
00:02:12,156 --> 00:02:13,964
A buy order swaps cash for coin.

66
00:02:14,484 --> 00:02:16,386
A sell order swaps coin back to

67
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:18,518
cash, and you can only sell coin you

68
00:02:18,518 --> 00:02:20,420
already hold, on a spot account.

69
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:22,577
A spot account is the normal

70
00:02:22,577 --> 00:02:23,929
account on an exchange.

71
00:02:24,449 --> 00:02:25,846
You own the coin you buy,

72
00:02:25,846 --> 00:02:27,187
and nothing is borrowed.

73
00:02:28,069 --> 00:02:29,838
A bot is software that places

74
00:02:29,838 --> 00:02:31,460
and refills orders for you.

75
00:02:31,980 --> 00:02:33,824
You start with some cash and some

76
00:02:33,824 --> 00:02:35,500
coin, so there is something to

77
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:37,232
buy with and something to sell.

78
00:02:37,281 --> 00:02:39,645
A grid bot places waiting buy orders

79
00:02:39,645 --> 00:02:41,774
on lines below the price and sell

80
00:02:41,774 --> 00:02:43,902
orders on lines above it, inside a

81
00:02:43,902 --> 00:02:45,636
top and a bottom you choose.

82
00:02:46,156 --> 00:02:47,832
The space between your top and

83
00:02:47,832 --> 00:02:49,620
your bottom is called the range.

84
00:02:49,714 --> 00:02:51,819
The sells need some coin, so a grid

85
00:02:51,819 --> 00:02:53,768
starts with part cash and part

86
00:02:53,768 --> 00:02:55,718
coin, and that is a description,

87
00:02:55,718 --> 00:02:57,589
not advice about what to hold.

88
00:02:58,639 --> 00:03:00,345
A limit order is an order that

89
00:03:00,345 --> 00:03:01,910
waits at a price you choose.

90
00:03:02,429 --> 00:03:03,993
It does not chase the price.

91
00:03:04,413 --> 00:03:05,977
Chasing the price would mean

92
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:07,430
moving the order to follow

93
00:03:07,430 --> 00:03:08,994
wherever the price has gone.

94
00:03:09,843 --> 00:03:11,918
An order fills when the price reaches

95
00:03:11,918 --> 00:03:13,650
its line and the trade happens.

96
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:16,318
Until then, the order is only waiting.

97
00:03:17,368 --> 00:03:19,323
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall.

98
00:03:19,465 --> 00:03:21,811
The rungs wait, and they do not chase you.

99
00:03:22,087 --> 00:03:24,377
A rung is one price where an order waits.

100
00:03:24,784 --> 00:03:26,963
The gap is the space between two rungs.

101
00:03:27,252 --> 00:03:29,297
The ladder is the analogy, and the

102
00:03:29,297 --> 00:03:31,568
chart beside it is the real past path.

103
00:03:32,618 --> 00:03:34,029
The range is the top rung

104
00:03:34,029 --> 00:03:35,158
and the bottom rung.

105
00:03:35,678 --> 00:03:37,801
The levels are the rungs between them.

106
00:03:38,151 --> 00:03:40,441
The stop is the written rule for leaving.

107
00:03:41,290 --> 00:03:43,134
The range is the top line and the

108
00:03:43,134 --> 00:03:44,977
bottom line, taken from the path.

109
00:03:45,456 --> 00:03:46,944
Hindsight: this range is

110
00:03:46,944 --> 00:03:48,209
drawn after the fact.

111
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:51,953
The chart is bitcoin's real daily

112
00:03:51,953 --> 00:03:55,523
closes from 19 July to 16 October 2023.

113
00:03:56,043 --> 00:03:57,495
Every close in this window

114
00:03:57,495 --> 00:03:59,227
stayed between those two lines.

115
00:04:00,013 --> 00:04:02,419
Six gaps of about 900 dollars each sit

116
00:04:02,419 --> 00:04:04,980
between the bottom line and the top line.

117
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,727
Each gap is about 900 dollars:

118
00:04:07,727 --> 00:04:09,954
the top line minus the bottom

119
00:04:09,954 --> 00:04:11,439
line, divided by six.

120
00:04:11,959 --> 00:04:13,304
It is one step between

121
00:04:13,304 --> 00:04:14,873
lines, not the whole range.

122
00:04:15,393 --> 00:04:17,231
Seven lines make those six gaps.

123
00:04:17,751 --> 00:04:19,539
The levels are the prices on the

124
00:04:19,539 --> 00:04:21,215
rungs where limit orders wait.

125
00:04:22,202 --> 00:04:24,492
Buy orders wait on lines below the price.

126
00:04:24,928 --> 00:04:26,883
Sell orders wait on lines above it.

127
00:04:27,365 --> 00:04:29,864
Each fill changes what you hold: a buy

128
00:04:29,864 --> 00:04:32,530
fill adds coin, and a sell fill adds cash.

129
00:04:33,050 --> 00:04:34,223
You choose the range,

130
00:04:34,223 --> 00:04:35,508
the gaps and the money.

131
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:37,269
The bot places each order.

132
00:04:38,276 --> 00:04:40,069
After a fill, the bot places the

133
00:04:40,069 --> 00:04:41,790
opposite order one rung away.

134
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:44,488
A buy fill gets a sell one rung higher.

135
00:04:44,875 --> 00:04:47,105
A sell fill gets a buy one rung lower.

136
00:04:47,625 --> 00:04:49,245
You still write the stop, and

137
00:04:49,245 --> 00:04:50,921
you act when that rule is met.

138
00:04:51,152 --> 00:04:53,387
The bot does not decide the stop for you

139
00:04:53,387 --> 00:04:55,510
unless you turned that setting on, and

140
00:04:55,510 --> 00:04:57,577
you write which one before you start.

141
00:04:58,311 --> 00:04:59,652
Think of a market stall.

142
00:05:00,084 --> 00:05:02,198
The stallholder buys stock a little

143
00:05:02,198 --> 00:05:04,312
cheaper and sells it a little dearer,

144
00:05:04,312 --> 00:05:05,932
and pays a fee on every sale.

145
00:05:06,383 --> 00:05:07,952
Exchanges charge a small

146
00:05:07,952 --> 00:05:08,998
fee on each trade.

147
00:05:09,518 --> 00:05:11,261
A grid can do that while price

148
00:05:11,261 --> 00:05:12,787
bounces inside the range.

149
00:05:13,307 --> 00:05:15,828
A bounce means price moves down and back

150
00:05:15,828 --> 00:05:18,197
up, or up and back down, and stays inside.

151
00:05:18,717 --> 00:05:20,953
One buy at a lower line and the later

152
00:05:20,953 --> 00:05:23,036
sell of that same coin is one pair.

153
00:05:23,556 --> 00:05:25,708
On these daily closes, the July to

154
00:05:25,708 --> 00:05:27,940
October example window finished

155
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:30,012
only three pairs one rung apart.

156
00:05:30,532 --> 00:05:32,264
The sell line is higher, so the

157
00:05:32,264 --> 00:05:34,108
cash that comes back is more than

158
00:05:34,108 --> 00:05:36,063
the cash that left, before the fee.

159
00:05:36,356 --> 00:05:37,809
A fee is what the exchange

160
00:05:37,809 --> 00:05:39,373
charges when an order fills.

161
00:05:39,554 --> 00:05:41,174
The fee comes out of the gap.

162
00:05:41,401 --> 00:05:43,133
If the fees are larger than the

163
00:05:43,133 --> 00:05:44,697
gap, the pair keeps nothing.

164
00:05:44,878 --> 00:05:46,121
This is not a promise.

165
00:05:46,641 --> 00:05:48,445
The pair finishes only if price

166
00:05:48,445 --> 00:05:50,318
does bounce and both orders fill.

167
00:05:51,368 --> 00:05:52,597
The daily close is the

168
00:05:52,597 --> 00:05:53,826
last price of the day.

169
00:05:54,247 --> 00:05:56,047
Crypto trades all day, so the

170
00:05:56,047 --> 00:05:57,456
day is cut at a set time.

171
00:05:57,976 --> 00:06:00,835
The exchange's day ends at 11am Sydney

172
00:06:00,835 --> 00:06:03,783
time in daylight saving, 10am otherwise.

173
00:06:04,303 --> 00:06:06,287
This is a simple candle that shows

174
00:06:06,287 --> 00:06:07,963
the day's high, low and close.

175
00:06:08,437 --> 00:06:10,366
Traders call it a candle because

176
00:06:10,366 --> 00:06:12,295
the full version has a thick body

177
00:06:12,295 --> 00:06:14,027
and a thin wick, like a candle.

178
00:06:14,459 --> 00:06:15,967
Here we only need the high,

179
00:06:15,967 --> 00:06:17,196
the low and the close.

180
00:06:17,530 --> 00:06:20,709
This candle is 19 July 2023.

181
00:06:21,229 --> 00:06:22,459
The high, the low, and

182
00:06:22,459 --> 00:06:23,743
the close are labelled.

183
00:06:24,636 --> 00:06:26,766
The example is Bitcoin's public

184
00:06:26,766 --> 00:06:28,421
daily price in US dollars.

185
00:06:28,941 --> 00:06:32,119
From 19 July 2023 to 16 October

186
00:06:32,119 --> 00:06:35,042
2023, every one of those days

187
00:06:35,042 --> 00:06:37,585
closed inside the range.

188
00:06:38,105 --> 00:06:39,778
The close crossed the seven

189
00:06:39,778 --> 00:06:41,524
lines 28 times in that window.

190
00:06:42,044 --> 00:06:44,355
The count is an example, not a forecast.

191
00:06:44,875 --> 00:06:46,663
We do not need to read each day.

192
00:06:46,929 --> 00:06:48,272
The shape is the lesson,

193
00:06:48,272 --> 00:06:49,685
and it is marked Example.

194
00:06:50,205 --> 00:06:52,961
Worked check: 19 July

195
00:06:52,961 --> 00:06:56,042
2023 to 16 October 2023.

196
00:06:56,562 --> 00:06:58,070
The low is the bottom line.

197
00:06:58,550 --> 00:07:00,016
The high is the top line.

198
00:07:00,536 --> 00:07:02,380
Nothing on this card is an order.

199
00:07:03,343 --> 00:07:06,186
Those 28 crossings, each time the price

200
00:07:06,186 --> 00:07:08,585
crosses a line, are not 28 results.

201
00:07:09,105 --> 00:07:11,307
A crossing only means the close moved

202
00:07:11,307 --> 00:07:13,374
from one side of a line to the other.

203
00:07:13,816 --> 00:07:15,528
A pair is finished only when a

204
00:07:15,528 --> 00:07:17,382
buy and its later sell have both

205
00:07:17,382 --> 00:07:19,113
filled, and only after the fee.

206
00:07:19,613 --> 00:07:21,512
The price can cross many lines and

207
00:07:21,512 --> 00:07:23,412
still leave you holding coin if it

208
00:07:23,412 --> 00:07:25,032
walks out through the bottom.

209
00:07:25,568 --> 00:07:27,077
You can buy part of a coin.

210
00:07:27,626 --> 00:07:30,585
Here we buy one hundredth

211
00:07:30,626 --> 00:07:31,687
of a bitcoin, 0.01.

212
00:07:31,687 --> 00:07:34,950
900 dollars times 0.01 bitcoin

213
00:07:34,950 --> 00:07:37,474
is 9 dollars before fees.

214
00:07:37,994 --> 00:07:40,975
In this example a buy waiting at the

215
00:07:40,975 --> 00:07:44,264
lower of these two lines was reached on

216
00:07:44,264 --> 00:07:47,245
17 August 2023, and the sell one line

217
00:07:47,245 --> 00:07:50,226
above was reached on 29 August 2023.

218
00:07:50,746 --> 00:07:52,534
The card shows the gap, then the

219
00:07:52,534 --> 00:07:54,098
two fees, then what is left.

220
00:07:54,407 --> 00:07:56,231
That is about 8 dollars 46

221
00:07:56,231 --> 00:07:58,317
after fees, for one small pair.

222
00:07:58,837 --> 00:08:00,736
It happens only if the price comes

223
00:08:00,736 --> 00:08:02,412
back up through the sell line.

224
00:08:02,516 --> 00:08:04,248
If the price leaves through the

225
00:08:04,248 --> 00:08:06,036
bottom, you still hold the coin,

226
00:08:06,036 --> 00:08:07,600
and the pair never finishes.

227
00:08:07,792 --> 00:08:09,580
This card is not money you made.

228
00:08:09,978 --> 00:08:12,324
Past results don't predict future results.

229
00:08:19,312 --> 00:08:21,100
Now watch what you hold when the

230
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:23,167
price leaves the range and stays out.

231
00:08:23,547 --> 00:08:25,223
Above the range the sells have

232
00:08:25,223 --> 00:08:27,010
filled and you are holding cash,

233
00:08:27,010 --> 00:08:28,463
with nothing left to sell.

234
00:08:28,785 --> 00:08:30,405
Below the range the buys have

235
00:08:30,405 --> 00:08:31,857
filled and you are holding

236
00:08:31,857 --> 00:08:33,589
coin, with nothing left to buy.

237
00:08:33,967 --> 00:08:35,359
That is why the way down

238
00:08:35,359 --> 00:08:37,117
matters most: every buy fills,

239
00:08:37,117 --> 00:08:38,875
and you are left holding coin.

240
00:08:40,925 --> 00:08:43,160
Here is that stop rule on the real path.

241
00:08:43,581 --> 00:08:45,926
It triggers if a daily close is outside

242
00:08:45,926 --> 00:08:48,271
the range, through the top or the bottom,

243
00:08:48,271 --> 00:08:50,762
and the next daily close is still outside.

244
00:08:51,282 --> 00:08:52,735
Then the idea is finished.

245
00:08:53,115 --> 00:08:55,208
You stop the bot, which cancels the

246
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:57,078
waiting orders, and do what you

247
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:59,172
wrote: keep the coin or swap to cash.

248
00:08:59,692 --> 00:09:01,673
A bot's automatic stop is a price

249
00:09:01,673 --> 00:09:03,361
that can fire during the day.

250
00:09:03,881 --> 00:09:05,581
This course uses the two daily

251
00:09:05,581 --> 00:09:07,416
closes, unless your written plan

252
00:09:07,416 --> 00:09:09,204
says you turned on a price stop.

253
00:09:09,636 --> 00:09:10,977
This is a teaching rule,

254
00:09:10,977 --> 00:09:12,155
not a recommendation.

255
00:09:12,675 --> 00:09:14,295
The stop is your written rule

256
00:09:14,295 --> 00:09:15,747
for when you stop the bot.

257
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:18,114
On 23 October 2023 the close

258
00:09:18,114 --> 00:09:20,526
finished above the top line, and

259
00:09:20,526 --> 00:09:22,845
the next day was still above it.

260
00:09:27,895 --> 00:09:29,347
Through the top, the sells

261
00:09:29,347 --> 00:09:31,023
have filled and you hold cash.

262
00:09:31,132 --> 00:09:32,976
Through the bottom, the buys have

263
00:09:32,976 --> 00:09:34,819
filled and you hold coin that you

264
00:09:34,819 --> 00:09:36,831
bought above where the price is now.

265
00:09:37,190 --> 00:09:38,642
That loss can keep growing

266
00:09:38,642 --> 00:09:39,759
until the stop acts.

267
00:09:40,064 --> 00:09:41,908
You stop the bot either way, then

268
00:09:41,908 --> 00:09:43,472
you follow the written rule.

269
00:09:43,581 --> 00:09:45,369
The bot does not decide the stop

270
00:09:45,369 --> 00:09:47,268
unless you turned that setting on.

271
00:09:47,541 --> 00:09:48,963
EXAMPLE, made up: three

272
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:50,542
buys fill on the way down.

273
00:09:51,062 --> 00:09:54,362
One hundredth of a bitcoin

274
00:09:54,362 --> 00:09:57,661
at 27,630 is 276 dollars 30.

275
00:09:58,515 --> 00:10:04,049
One hundredth at 26,730 is 267 dollars 30.

276
00:10:04,901 --> 00:10:10,083
One hundredth at 25,830 is 258 dollars 30.

277
00:10:10,603 --> 00:10:13,243
